## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical zero-trust for admin access, mirroring real enterprise risk of credential theft and lateral movement in hybrid environments.

## Key Concepts
- Zero-trust, device posture, MFA, PIM, Just-In-Time
- Jump hosts, session recording, RBAC, break-glass, SIEM/audit

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-policy: grant only if posture true and MFA passed
if (device.posture && user.mfa && time.inWindow) {
  grantAccess();
} else {
  denyAccess();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure effectiveness (MTTR, number of break-glass events)?
- How would this adapt to cloud-native IAM vs PAM solutions across AWS/Azure?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes data sovereignty, cross-cloud cryptographic governance, and incident readiness in a fintech setting, pushing candidates to map CISSP controls to multi-cloud realities.

## Key Concepts

- Data classification and residency
- Cross-cloud KMS integration and key lifecycle
- Access control and auditability
- Incident response and evidence handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// policy-as-code gate example (pseudocode)
function enforcePolicy(data) {
  if (data.classification === 'PCI' && data.region !== 'allowed') {
    throw new Error('Residency violation');
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the key rotation policy in prod?
- How do you handle secrets exposure risk in this design?
